  "reason": "Complete construction and prerequisite audit; see research/phase-2-next-20-batch-4.notes.md and coverage.json. Source D, Example 4.2.1 pp.217–218; documented alternative-proof disposition, no raw fetch claim. The generated-sigma-algebra construction gives a filtration and adapted sums. Finite L1 closure establishes integrability. Group independence separates sigma(Y_{n+1}) from sigma(Y_1,...,Y_n); the independent-variable conditioning lemma gives E[Y_{n+1}|F_n]=0. Condition the known S_n and add the next increment. No identical distribution, variance, or infinite-product construction is required: the independent sequence is given. AC is inherited from the Radon–Nikodym construction of conditional expectation; if a sequence of versions is needed, AC selects measurable versions at the countably many times. Identities remain identities of almost-sure classes, without completing the filtration. For fixed n, the sums S_1,...,S_n are measurable functions of Y_1,...,Y_n, and Y_k=S_k-S_{k-1} with S_0=c; minimality of generated sigma-algebras therefore proves equality of these two finite-history sigma-algebras.",
